A. Theorem Q2.1: wrong outputs stay O(K) when V has no total blind spot
   m = 400 kinds, Zipf(1.1) frequencies over 70% of problems (30% routine); 20 seeds;
   'bound' is c * rejections (reruns succeed here, so the +1 term is 0).
   uniform: w = 0.5, f = 0.4                               c = 0.25; product-class bound sum_k c_k = 100
      T =   1000: wrong outputs     37.0 (rate 0.0370), rejections   151.6, bound c*R = 38
      T =  10000: wrong outputs     93.7 (rate 0.0094), rejections   372.1, bound c*R = 93
      T = 100000: wrong outputs     97.1 (rate 0.0010), rejections   400.0, bound c*R = 100
      last 10% of T = 1e5 (seed 0): failure rate 0.0000, rejection rate 0.0000, (c+1) x rejection rate 0.0000
   heterogeneous: w ~ U[.3,.9], f ~ U[.2,.95]              c = 3.77; product-class bound sum_k c_k = 266
      T =   1000: wrong outputs     76.5 (rate 0.0765), rejections   134.2, bound c*R = 506
      T =  10000: wrong outputs    218.8 (rate 0.0219), rejections   356.8, bound c*R = 1344
      T = 100000: wrong outputs    259.6 (rate 0.0026), rejections   399.9, bound c*R = 1507
      last 10% of T = 1e5 (seed 0): failure rate 0.0000, rejection rate 0.0000, (c+1) x rejection rate 0.0000
   one pure blind spot (kind 6: w = f = 1)                 c = inf; product-class bound sum_k c_k = inf
      T =   1000: wrong outputs     54.9 (rate 0.0549), rejections   150.6, bound c*R = inf
      T =  10000: wrong outputs    287.4 (rate 0.0287), rejections   371.1, bound c*R = inf
      T = 100000: wrong outputs   2008.0 (rate 0.0201), rejections   399.0, bound c*R = inf
      last 10% of T = 1e5 (seed 0): failure rate 0.0190, rejection rate 0.0000, (c+1) x rejection rate inf
   unmasking: hidden 2nd layer w = 1, f = 0.9              c = 9.00; product-class bound sum_k c_k = 3644
      T =   1000: wrong outputs    217.7 (rate 0.2177), rejections   183.5, bound c*R = 1652
      T =  10000: wrong outputs   1364.8 (rate 0.1365), rejections   525.7, bound c*R = 4731
      T = 100000: wrong outputs   3429.7 (rate 0.0343), rejections   781.6, bound c*R = 7034
      last 10% of T = 1e5 (seed 0): failure rate 0.0045, rejection rate 0.0007, (c+1) x rejection rate 0.0070
   30% problem-specific (fresh) kinds, w = 0.5, f = 0.4    c = 0.25; product-class bound sum_k c_k = 100
      T =   1000: wrong outputs     91.5 (rate 0.0915), rejections   360.9, bound c*R = 90
      T =  10000: wrong outputs    688.4 (rate 0.0688), rejections  2737.5, bound c*R = 684
      T = 100000: wrong outputs   6110.6 (rate 0.0611), rejections 24422.8, bound c*R = 6106
      last 10% of T = 1e5 (seed 0): failure rate 0.0589, rejection rate 0.2377, (c+1) x rejection rate 0.2971
   Reading: with no total blind spot the total stays near c*m whatever T, so the rate
   falls like K/T; a pure blind spot or problem-specific kinds make it linear in T.

B. Theorem Q2.3: falsification by use bounds reliance on false outputs by K/(b e)
   m = 200 kinds over all problems (Zipf 1.1); V passes every wrong claim of the first
   50 kinds (w = f = 1: a pure blind spot) and catches the rest (f = 0); each problem
   cites u = 3 uniform earlier outputs; a cited false output is exposed w.p. e, which is
   a hit; the library is recomputed (outputs of a learned kind become correct). 20 seeds.
   e = 0.05: uses of false outputs  1019.5 (bound K/(b e) with 50 blind kinds:  1000), exposures 50.0, wrong outputs released 383.4
   e = 0.20: uses of false outputs   263.5 (bound K/(b e) with 50 blind kinds:   250), exposures 50.0, wrong outputs released 138.2
   e = 0.50: uses of false outputs   102.0 (bound K/(b e) with 50 blind kinds:   100), exposures 50.0, wrong outputs released 83.4
   Without uses (e = 0) every blind-kind problem is a wrong output for ever: about
   81% of problems.

C. Thread U's P(works) with the rejection budget of Theorem 5(b) imposed
   (same draws as threadU_verify.p_works; 'orig' must reproduce its model figures).
   orig : F = p w rbar f with p ~ U[.1,.5] independent of T/K ~ logU[3,30]
   cap  : p <= 1/(T/K (1 - w f)), since rejections <= K (b = 1) under (A2), (A3');
          mixed f, i.e. learning does not shift the error mix (no allocation)
   kinds: F <= rbar * cbar / (T/K), cbar = sum_tau share_tau w f_tau/(1 - w f_tau):
          Theorem Q2.1(b), each kind of error bounded separately (allocation allowed)
   worst: as cap, with every error of the protocol's hardest type from the start
   kinds, beta=0.1: as kinds, with audits cut from one per output to 0.1 (Theorem Q2.1
          bounds wrong outputs without audits when V has no total blind spot)
   math       V-human: one expert reads (unlocated verdict)      orig 35% (threadU 35%) cap 48% kinds 47% worst 30% kinds,beta=0.1 55% | output ok 54%->79%, effort ok 74% | f 0.43, worst f 0.92, cbar 0.24
   math       read + AI critics (3)                              orig 64% (threadU 64%) cap 74% kinds 73% worst 49% kinds,beta=0.1 78% | output ok 78%->90%, effort ok 94% | f 0.18, worst f 0.87, cbar 0.10
   math       LEAN: machine + AI critics (3) + adversarial read  orig 62% (threadU 62%) cap 71% kinds 70% worst 45% kinds,beta=0.1 76% | output ok 82%->93%, effort ok 92% | f 0.15, worst f 0.86, cbar 0.09
   software   fixed acceptance tests only (folder's test-suite r orig 39% (threadU 39%) cap 63% kinds 59% worst 30% kinds,beta=0.1 59% | output ok 45%->68%, effort ok 100% | f 0.45, worst f 1.00, cbar 0.38
   software   LEAN: tests + independent tests + fuzzing + AI cri orig 73% (threadU 73%) cap 79% kinds 78% worst 48% kinds,beta=0.1 82% | output ok 88%->94%, effort ok 95% | f 0.07, worst f 0.81, cbar 0.05
   empirical  V-human: one expert reads (unlocated)              orig  9% (threadU  9%) cap 11% kinds 11% worst  9% kinds,beta=0.1 13% | output ok 18%->30%, effort ok 69% | f 0.70, worst f 0.95, cbar 1.19
   empirical  FAST: rerun + re-analysis + AI critics (3) + read  orig 23% (threadU 23%) cap 28% kinds 26% worst 15% kinds,beta=0.1 30% | output ok 51%->61%, effort ok 76% | f 0.27, worst f 0.85, cbar 0.38
   emp-narrow FAST: rerun + re-analysis + AI critics (3) + read  orig 28% (threadU 28%) cap 34% kinds 31% worst 15% kinds,beta=0.1 36% | output ok 61%->71%, effort ok 76% | f 0.17, worst f 0.85, cbar 0.24
   judgment   the same + fact checks                             orig 28% (threadU 28%) cap 36% kinds 32% worst 16% kinds,beta=0.1 36% | output ok 53%->62%, effort ok 82% | f 0.21, worst f 0.85, cbar 0.38
   share of no-transfer draws with p (1 - wf) T > K, at wf = 0.19: 82%
   share of no-transfer draws with p (1 - wf) T > K, at wf = 0.45: 66%
   Reading: thread U samples p and T/K independently, so most of its no-transfer draws
   need more rejections than Theorem 5(b) allows. Imposing the budget raises every row
   whose binding constraint was output failure. Counting errors kind by kind keeps most
   of the gain; only the extreme 'all errors of the hardest type' reading erases it.

